  </div></div></section><div class="pf">
  <section id="p1" class="pf-r"><div class="w"><div class="pf-in">
    <img class="pf-img" src="/brand-assets/mockup-team/catherine-palmer.png" alt="Catherine Palmer">
    <div>
      <div class="pf-idx"><i></i><span>01 · Editor-in-Chief</span></div>
      <div class="pf-n">Catherine Palmer</div>
      <div class="pf-meta"><span>Indianapolis</span><span>15+ years in editorial leadership</span><span>Politics &amp; federal courts</span></div>
      <p class="pf-q">If we cannot show a reader how we know something, we have not finished reporting it.</p>
      <p class="pf-x">Catherine leads the newsroom from Indianapolis. Her career spans more than fifteen years in editorial leadership at regional and national publications, with a background that includes reporting on politics, state government, and federal courts before she moved into editing. She sets the standards for what runs on the site, oversees the corrections record, and is the final authority on questions of what America’s News Today will and will not publish.</p>
    </div>
  </div></div></section>
  <section id="p2" class="pf-r"><div class="w"><div class="pf-in">
    <div>
      <div class="pf-idx"><i></i><span>02 · Managing Editor</span></div>
      <div class="pf-n">Nicholas Griffin</div>
      <div class="pf-meta"><span>Tampa</span><span>12 years at a regional daily</span><span>Calendar &amp; assignments</span></div>
      <p class="pf-q">A newsroom runs on clear communication and deadlines people can actually meet.</p>
      <p class="pf-x">Nicholas manages the day-to-day operations of the newsroom from Tampa. He came to the publication after twelve years at a Southern regional daily, where he rose from city desk reporter to assistant managing editor with stops on the politics and copy desks. He is responsible for the editorial calendar, story assignments, and the flow of publication across the desks.</p>
    </div>
    <img class="pf-img" src="/brand-assets/mockup-team/nicholas-griffin.png" alt="Nicholas Griffin">
  </div></div></section>
  <section id="p3" class="pf-r"><div class="w"><div class="pf-in">
    <img class="pf-img" src="/brand-assets/mockup-team/denise-chapman.png" alt="Denise Chapman">
    <div>
      <div class="pf-idx"><i></i><span>03 · Business Editor</span></div>
      <div class="pf-n">Denise Chapman</div>
      <div class="pf-meta"><span>Grand Rapids</span><span>A decade on the beat</span><span>Business, finance &amp; labor</span></div>
      <p class="pf-q">Read the filing first. The press release is an argument, not a fact.</p>
      <p class="pf-x">Denise runs the business and economy desk from Grand Rapids. Her reporting career includes more than a decade covering business, finance, and labor at regional daily newspapers and a national business publication. She is the editor most likely to reach for the underlying numbers on a story and the one who insists on distinguishing what a company has actually announced from what its press release wants readers to think it announced.</p>
    </div>
  </div></div></section>
  <section id="p4" class="pf-r"><div class="w"><div class="pf-in">
    <div>
      <div class="pf-idx"><i></i><span>04 · Publisher</span></div>
      <div class="pf-n">Scott Coleman</div>
      <div class="pf-meta"><span>Dallas</span><span>Media &amp; business operations</span><span>No editorial input</span></div>
      <p class="pf-q">My job is to fund the newsroom and keep the commercial side out of it.</p>
      <p class="pf-x">Scott is the publisher of America’s News Today, working from Dallas. His background is in media and business operations, and he holds responsibility for the site’s overall direction, financial sustainability, and the independence of the editorial operation from the commercial side of the site. He leaves the day-to-day editorial decisions to the newsroom and writes an occasional column on the business of journalism.</p>
    </div>
    <img class="pf-img" src="/brand-assets/mockup-team/scott-coleman.png" alt="Scott Coleman">
  </div></div></section></div><section class="jn"><div class="w"><div class="jn-in">
